CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^.*invalid implicit conversion.*to 'struct myopt'.*$
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
Verifies that a user-defined conversion sequence may select a
function-template converting constructor.

Per [over.match.copy]/1 + [over.ics.user] + [temp.deduct]: a
converting constructor that is a function template participates in
copy-initialization once its template arguments are deduced.

Without the fix, CBMC's template-constructor fallback in
`user_defined_conversion_sequence` accepted the instantiated
constructor only if it carried `ID_specialization_of` (the CLASS
template-specialization tag).  A member converting-constructor
function template's instantiation instead carries
`#fn_template_args`, so the valid instantiation was rejected and
the conversion failed with "invalid implicit conversion from 'T'
to 'struct myopt'".

This mirrors `std::optional<T>`'s `optional(_Up&&)` converting
constructor, which CBMC's own source relies on when returning a
`T` into a `std::optional<T>`.
